  "details": "I staff for groups and I have all my staff friended so that I can tell where there at and if they are online or not. But my actual friends, I have another account that I have them friended on so I don't get staff and friends mixed up. My idea is if we can take and have where we can assign our friends a color for their names so instead of being white for non friended and yellow for friends, it be white for non friended and let's say category 1 I can set the name colors to be blue, category 2 can be red, and category 3 can be green etc. so I can take and put my staff from adultfurrs in group 1 which makes their name be green or something like that and my other group staff I can put in another group with color.. \n\nAlso I may suggest to go along with this feature to have when we send them a friend request, it will ask what category to put them in upon accepted automatically. So that when the friend accepts, it will auto be put in the designated category. ATM you guys call the categories I am referring as groups. I called them categories so they don't get mixed up as actual groups.",
